{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T17:15:46.601Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1781+pm-gh1787+pm-glmcnd+pm-jzrtsr","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rzojed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Secret guard misses a credential inside a POSIX recovery command whose argument the renderer single-quoted with apostrophe splices"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"quotePosixCommandArg single-quotes an argument that holds !, CR or LF, or ends in a backslash (pm-oq893h, pm-jzrtsr), and spells each apostrophe in it as the splice '\\''. When such an argument holds a key-named assignment whose value is itself quoted (a note with a line break and a quoted password-style assignment), the detector judges the rendered command, sees the key inside the first single-quoted piece and the value starting at a closing quote, and reports nothing; it reports the same argument raw and in the double-quoted spelling main rendered before line breaks were single-quoted. The gap existed for !-holding arguments since pm-oq893h and widened with pm-jzrtsr. Found by the Codex round 4 review of PR #1789."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:security","recovery","secret-guard","shell-quoting"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-26T17:15:46.601Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T17:15:46.601Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The detector reads a POSIX single-quoted word with '\\'' splices as the shell word it spells before judging a key-named assignment inside it; A rendered recovery command, raw and inside a JSON string, carries the same findings as its unrendered argument for every spelling quotePosixCommandArg emits; A differential against the published bundle shows no other verdict change"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A credential in an argument is reported in the rendered recovery command whatever quoting the renderer chose"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"An argument with a line break or ! and a quoted credential assignment is reported raw but not in its single-quoted rendering"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1781","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-26T17:15:46.601Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-jzrtsr","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-26T17:15:46.601Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-oq893h","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-26T17:15:46.601Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"befor